From 72360dfbb545a2b4d01ae458ad2d56a2b837514a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 03:03:08 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(motion): Face opens with an approach rapid on the
 clearance plane

The facer started its path at the entry point in the air, so its first
move was the plunge. Posts write a move's end only, so the first posted
motion was a 3-axis feed from the tool-change position straight to cutting
depth. Face now starts its cursor where the other mill generators do and
rapids to the entry at clearance before the plunge. An entry at exactly
X0 Y0 states that approach as a zero-length rapid.

Goldens regenerated: the face .cl goldens and every dialect's .nc
(including program_entry pause/home) gain the G00 approach; regression
move/line counts and minutes take the one extra rapid; the fixture-law
test names the approach beside the plunge.

Fixes #690

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
